the ocean is a large mysterious scary  thing many horror stories and  supernatural sightings come from tales  of the deep such as sightings of a large  tentacle monster called the Kraken or  warnings of beautiful serenading  mermaids that pull sailors to the depths  to be eaten alive whether or not these  legends are real stories or just the  drunken recollections of fatigued  sailors their impact can be felt in the  hearts of every person who dares to sail  into unknown waters one of these brave  souls is none other than link from the  Wind Waker to no surprise the Zelda  universe has its own fair share of  supernatural legends and superstitions  but in the Wind Waker which mainly  features a large untamed ocean some of  these stories have come true at one  point in links adventure the courageous  hero is tasked with finding the pieces  of the Triforce of courage which have  been scattered throughout Hyrule after  the hero of time departed from the land  these pieces can be found by deciphering  charts that depict their locations  buried in chests at the bottom of the  sea but one of these triforce charts is  held in a chilling location legend has  it that on nights when the moon is  present an eerie green storm will take  the skies and a solemn haunting tune can  be heard wailing across the waves coming  from a ship with tattered sails sailing  without a single living soul aboard  those who are unfortunate enough to see  this curse at vessel refer to it as the  ghost ship truly one of the most  terrifying pieces of Zelda lore but a  ship with such importance to the hero's  journey and the will of the goddesses  must have some prior significance which  is hidden to us in present time so  without further ado follow me as we dive  deep into the mysteries underneath the  ghost ship  not much is revealed openly about this  ship in-game but what we are able to  find out is downright terrifying the  ghost ship will appear every night in a  different location across the Great Sea  depending on the lunar cycle of the moon  however to approach the ship without it  disappearing from sight once you get  near it  one must have in their possession the  ghost ship chart this is a mysterious  chart that seems to hold some magical  self-awareness  enabling it to indicate exactly what  step the moon is on in its cycle and  therefore where the ghost ship is  sailing upon that night  once link has obtained the ghost ship  chart the ship will no longer disappear  upon approaching it and can successfully  be boarded well if you call being warped  into its interior boarding according to  the eccentric adventurer photographer  man named Lenz Oh who has successfully  taken a picture of the ghost ship and  survived to tell the tale the chart was  made by an unknown man who quote  research to the reaches of the sea with  a ghost ship faded in and out of sight  and that he drew a map of his movements  but it is said that as soon as the man  had finished drawing the lines of that  cursed map he died a most unexpected  death whether it was the curse of the  ghost ship that doomed him to an early  grave or some other unfortunate means it  is heavily implied to be the former of  the two furthermore the chart is found  in a chest underneath of a diamond step  island in a hidden ship graveyard that  forms a complex maze once the chart is  obtained the next step is for link to  track it down and climb aboard when the  seas turn a sickly green and it begins  to storm you know the ship is nearby  there are a few important things to note  about its appearance firstly the ship  bears very strong resemblances to tetras  pirate ship in fact they're almost  exactly alike the colorations are  different though with tetris featuring  brighter red colors and the ghost ship  more of a faded mossy green palette both  ships feature artwork on the head of the  ship which do differ as well with Tetris  featuring the head of a serpent or  dragon and the ghost ships featuring  what appears to be an outward reaching  praying woman  the ship is also covered by what appears  to be flying blue flames which have been  indicated in other Zelda games such as  ocarina of time breath of the wild and  Twilight Princess to be what spirits  look like once inside the interior is  rather plain and resembles that of a  submarine from other portions of the  Great Sea but there are a few more  details in its interior that are rather  peculiar along the right wall there's a  beam of light that is seeping in through  a crack somewhere and where it shines a  lone white flower is blooming the floor  is lined with a ghastly mist and the  ceiling is cracked open permitting you  to see ghostly spirits surrounding the  chamber you're in indicating this is  some different plane of existence from  where you are physically in the Great  Sea hanging just above the treasure  chest which is accessible after  defeating the monsters within the ship a  strange portrait of a face is present  this face emits a demonic terrifying  grin that disappears into an  expressionless face when link walks  closer and finally the chest holds a  Triforce chart which reveals the  location of one of the eight shards of  the Triforce of courage in the HD remake  it has been replaced with just  straight-up a shard of the Triforce of  courage after link picks up the treasure  a sudden painful sounding yell is heard  and Link's consciousness fades to black  when he wakes up he's aboard the king of  Red Lions and the ghost ship is never to  be seen or heard of again okay now that  we're all in the same page with the ship  let's start piecing together what all  this madness could mean the entire  purpose of the vessel is to guard one of  the shards of the Triforce of courage as  indicated by what's in its treasure  chest and the fact that it no longer  haunts the Seas once link obtains said  treasure the Triforce as mentioned  before was shattered into eight pieces  once the hero of time left Hyrule it's  believed that the Triforce was shattered  to hide it away this seems to indicate  that the ship and its crew were  commissioned by the goddesses to guard  the shard of the Triforce from those who  would seek it for evil such as Ganon  it's possible that the ship is actually  an evil entity who is keeping the shard  from link in order to serve Ganon but  that doesn't make too much sense since  ganador actually wants all pieces of the  Triforce for himself and if it were a  haunted vessel by his doing he would  simply take the shard for himself by  this point but what the goddesses really  command a vessel  be haunted for all eternity and even  release monsters incited to guard the  Triforce yard well to be honest this is  the same game that revealed the  goddesses in their benevolence to have  literally flooded the entire world and  efforts to kill Ganondorf meaning they  are no strangers to taking drastic  sometimes tragic measures for the  greater good  so drafting a ship into eternal service  seems pretty plausible as well we also  see from other Zelda titles that's  serving the goddesses after death is  rather common especially among the  sheikah clan but even if the ghost ship  was made by the goddesses for righteous  purposes who were the poor souls made to  service the goddesses for all eternity  and why did the man charting the ship's  locations died unexpectedly and whose  spirits are these that we can see  floating around the vessel well as far  as those floating spirits go they are  actually the spirits of dead seagulls  that have been tied to the ship seagulls  are shown in game to fly around Tetris  ship and even the tiny king of Red Lions  and these unfortunate birds were bound  for all eternity to haunt the Seas  alongside the ghost ship but the ship  was once manned by a crew that much is  certain although I believe the answer to  who those individuals were may not be  what you're expecting let's recap our  Clues so far the ghost ship resembles  Tetris ship very closely in both build  and design as well as every other ship  in the graveyard we see underneath  diamond step Island these ruined ships  are further tied to the ghost ship due  to the fact that they house the ghost  ship chart these and Tetris ship are the  only vessels in the entire game that  resemble one another and they do so with  almost suspicious accuracy Tetris ship  has been in her family bloodline for at  least two generations since we know that  before her leadership it was her mother  who was captain tetra is later revealed  to be zelda spoiler warning I guess and  we can see a portrait of the hero of  time in her chambers inside the ship who  was only depicted one other time in the  submerged hyrule castle leading to the  next logical question of why and how she  would have this picture at all  considering her royal history and this  strangely added image of the ancient  hero of time could it be that tetra ship  is actually from old Hyrule would've  all those ships resembling Tetris pirate  ship are actually from the old Hylian  fleet that rose to the surface under the  goddesses protection when Hyrule was  flooded long ago and that is when the  Princess Zelda of that time be it tetras  mother or grandmother or whoever in  order to save her own bloodline became a  pirate alongside the ancestors of her  current pirate crew relating this back  to the ghost ship it could be just one  of the other ships in the fleet that had  then been given the task of rowing the  Seas for all eternity protecting the  shard of the Triforce with the souls of  the entire remaining haile and sailors  bound to the vessel explaining the  rather large number of ghostly  apparitions that can be seen along the  floors and ceiling inside the ship the  goddesses then took the remaining ships  from the fleet and hid them away in a  large ship's graveyard maze hiding the  ghost ship chart as far as why the man  from lenses legend who drew the chart  died unexpectedly for all we know this  could just be a frightening legend since  it's unlikely a mere mortal man could  create the chart with its magical  properties in the first place  with the ships origins crew and curse  explained I think that wraps up this  mystery pretty well but what do you  think does the ghost ship have another  origin let me know in the comments below  thank you all so much for watching as  always it's been a blast working on this  theory and it was of course exciting to  get to share it with you be sure to LIKE  this video if you liked it and subscribe  if you haven't already for much more  Zelda and Nintendo content to come huge  thank you to my amazing patrons of which  I have two new additions welcome to  Thomas McClure and Amanda mull so you  guys are amazing and I'm so honored to  have you in my videos if you're  interested in getting your name up here  at the end of all my videos follow the  link in the description below to find  out how also down there are links to my  Twitter and discord and you know other  places to get in touch with me directly  so be sure to check that out too that's  all I've got for you today so as always  I hope you have a phenomenal rest of  this is massimino bandit signing out  [Music]
 

